* [http://people.fix.no/arj/lojban/lojban-ispell-hashfile.html|ispell data files] - Data files to allow Lojban spell checking with ispell
* [http://go.to/jbofihe|jbofi'e] - The ''de facto'' standard parser and glosser for Lojban. Mirrored on [http://www.digitalkingdom.org/cvsweb/jbofihe/
**] ((lujvo expander)) in python that uses vlatai from jbofi'e.
** the ''de jure'' standard parser remains the dos version in the old Lojban files mentioned below.
* [http://www.tomeraider.com|Tomeraider] files containing the ((gismu)) list (English and Lojban ordering), the ((cmavo)) list (((cmavo)) and ((selma'o)) ordering), the ((rafsi)) list and the ((BNF)) grammar, for [http://www.tlg.uci.edu/~opoudjis/dist/lojban.tr.zip|PC] and [http://www.tlg.uci.edu/~opoudjis/dist/lojban.pdb.zip|Palm Pilot]
* ((Jay Kominek))'s [http://ucsub.colorado.edu/~kominek/lojban/flashlojban.pl|Perl flashcard script] (It requires some other software on [http://ucsub.colorado.edu/~kominek/lojban/|his Lojban page] to generate the data files)
*There has been some interest in constructing a Lojban text-based Adventure-style game.
**((Nick Nicholas)) translated the text of ''[http://www.rickadams.org/adventure/|Colossal Cave]'' in 1991.  ((Robin Lee Powell)) has heroically translated that translation into a working game - see the ''[http://www.lojban.org/cgi-bin/twiki/view/Files/Programs|Community Files Area]'' on the TWiki for that, and also for the Inform Localisation files needed to create your own Lojbanic IF.
**There is a proposal here for a new game in the works, ((lojbo munje)).
*[http://www.ice.ru/~slobin/vim/syntax/lojban.vim|lojban.vim] enables lojban syntax highlighting while using [http://www.vim.org/|vim] text editor.
*[http://www.emacswiki.org/cgi-bin/wiki.pl?LojbanMode|lojban-mode] syntax highlighting and other support code for emacs
*Various software (DOS, primarily) is described and accessible at [http://www.lojban.org/files/roadmap.html#software], including Logflash, the most effect vocabulary learning aid still, and the official parser.
*[http://www.digitalkingdom.org/~bjoern/Popup|Popup.app] is a [http://www.gnustep.org|GNUstep] based vocabulary learning tool that can use cmafi'e to extract the vocabulary from a given text.
* ((FlashCards)), a Macintosh program
** some data for it is available at [http://satirist.org/lojban/cilre/
*] ((A simple perl script for grepping the word lists with colorized output)) by ((Jordan DeLong))

!Web-accessible Software

* [http://valfahi.balvi.org|valfa'i] - An online dictionary.
* [http://www.barsoom.net/lojban/gloss/masmuni.cgi|macmavo] - A glossing program.
* [http://www.epita.fr/~poss_r/lojban/jboski.html|jbofi'e online] - A web based version of jbofi'e
* [http://www.codedbliss.com/lojban/zanfahi/|zanfa'i] - Another online dictionary, also for download.
* [http://www.codedbliss.com/lojban/selylergahi/|selylerga'i] - online lojban orthography convertor (currently Latin -> Arabic, Tengwar, Turkish, or IPA).

